answer:
Add a stdio server entry to your agent’s MCP configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "colony": {
      "command": "colony",
      "args": ["--home", "/absolute/path/to/agent-home", "mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

Use an absolute executable path if `colony` is not on your PATH, and an absolute home path. The server provides `ask(question, namespace?)` and `push(namespace, question, content, sources?, tainted?)` tools. [README.md](/C:/Users/b3vel/Documents/Codex/2026-10-20/https-github-com-vivaannarayana-colony-https/work/benchmark-remediation-live-51-runtime/main/repo/README.md:65)

Add this entry to your MCP configuration, replacing the home path with your agent’s absolute home path:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "colony": {
      "command": "colony",
      "args": ["--home", "/absolute/path/to/agent-home", "mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

Use an absolute executable path if `colony` is not on `PATH`. ([README.md](/README.md:66))

